Negative control for the scope catch-all every scenario route ends in.

Narrows `SCOPE_SUFFIX_SEGMENT` to a single dynamic segment, so a registered
route still serves `/useClientEmails/as/client` and stops matching the
`/for/:type/:id` retarget entirely. This is the silent shape the design's 4.2.2
probe warned about: the url still works, the actor still parses, and
`.for('client', id)` simply never arrives — FE-2824's failure mode arriving by
way of the router.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds (module lane, measured 2026-08-11 — 10 failed, 8 passed, of which 2
failures are the pre-existing declared-nav gap this mutant does not touch):
  scenario-routes.spec.ts   "ends every scenario path in the scope catch-all"
                            + all five "@G3d the four scope shapes still
                              resolve" cases
  scenario-nav-routes.spec.ts
                            "derives a link for the canary and excludes its
                              handoff target (R8)"
                            "leaves no derived link unmatched by the router"

The collision lane stays green, which is the point: the two guards are
independent, and narrowing the suffix is invisible to the one that only reads
route names.

